--- a/docs/spec/hardware-dm32.md
+++ b/docs/spec/hardware-dm32.md
@@ -1592,6 +1592,6 @@
 
 ## Receive past the rated bands
 
-16-65, 174-400 and 480-1120 MHz: receive only in FM, enabled by default in this fork ([radio-features.md](radio-features.md) 6.2). Through 740 MHz this follows the FD6818 band table (8.3). The 740-1120 MHz extension is experimental: it reuses the top band-select words, whose row also ends at 1120 MHz in the related FD6818SH driver, but no sensitivity, synthesizer lock or real reception has been measured on a DM-32UV.
+16-65, 174-400 and 480-1120 MHz: receive only in FM, while **Tools > RX past bands** is On ([radio-features.md](radio-features.md) 6.2). The option is Off on a first start and after a factory reset; the saved choice survives a restart. Through 740 MHz this follows the FD6818 band table (8.3). The 740-1120 MHz extension is experimental: it reuses the top band-select words, whose row also ends at 1120 MHz in the related FD6818SH driver, but no sensitivity, synthesizer lock or real reception has been measured on a DM-32UV.
 
 The VFO accepts nine digits above 1 GHz (`112000000` = 1120.00000 MHz); existing entries of up to eight digits keep their 3+5 MHz/decimal meaning. Channel records remain limited to 999.999990 MHz by their eight-BCD-digit 10 Hz fields, so GHz reception is VFO-only rather than truncating a channel to another frequency. PTT remains denied throughout every receive-only extension.
--- a/docs/spec/radio-features.md
+++ b/docs/spec/radio-features.md
@@ -748,7 +748,7 @@
 
 | Rule | Detail |
 |---|---|
-| Setting | Settings > Advanced > RX past bands. Stored in `settings_t.cp_flags`; a factory reset returns it to its default, which `CONFIG_RX_EXT_ON` sets (on in this tree, off in RadioFoundry's). Hidden on a board with no range. Older stored settings take the enabled default once when this build first loads them. The owner can turn it off after that. |
+| Setting | **Tools > RX past bands** toggles it directly; the same switch remains in Settings > Advanced. Stored in `settings_t.cp_flags`; a factory reset returns it to the default selected by `CONFIG_RX_EXT_ON` (the DM-32UV sets it off). Both rows are hidden on a board with no range. Older stored settings take an enabled default once when such a build first loads them; an owner's explicit On or Off choice survives later boots. |
 | Table | Everything that reads the bands uses `board_band_count()`: the VFO's tuning and wrap, the keypad entry, VFO scan, the channel editor, `rigctld` and the debug link's `bands=`. |
 | Transmit | Never: `board_in_band(hz, true)` skips the entries, so PTT gives `TXDENY_BAND`. |
 | Modes | FM only, as in any receive-only band: the channel editor refuses DMR there. |
